NAME:2026-multifaith-calendar-Victoria
CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-7622218@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260104
SUMMARY:Mahayana New Year
DESCRIPTION:Mahayana New Year starts on the first full moon day in January. Celebrated in Mahayana countries like China\, Korea\, Japan\, Taiwan and Vietnam. A time to reflect on the past and to make a fresh start.\nReligion: Buddhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-5080525@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260105
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260106
SUMMARY:Birthday of Guru Gobind Singh Ji 
DESCRIPTION:Commemorates the birth of Guru Gobind Singh (1666-1708)\, the tenth and final Sikh Guru\, who created the collective body of baptised Sikhs (Khalsa) and declared the Sikh Scriptures (Guru Granth Sahib) to be the Sikh's Guru from that time on.\nReligion: Sikhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-1644419@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260107
SUMMARY:Epiphany
DESCRIPTION:Epiphany commemorates the manifestation of God in human form as Jesus Christ\, and the visit of the three wise men to the infant Jesus. Celebrated 12 days after Christmas.\nReligion: Christianity
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-3355293@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260108
SUMMARY:Nativity [Orthodox]
DESCRIPTION:Nativity is the Orthodox celebration of the birth of Jesus Christ\, considered by Christians to be the Son of God. Celebrated by Orthodox churches that follow the Julian calendar.\nReligion: Christianity
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-8770362@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260113
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260114
SUMMARY:Maghi 
DESCRIPTION:Maghi commemorates the sacrifice of forty Sikhs\, who sacrificed their lives defending an attack by the imperial army in pursuit of Guru Gobind Singh\, in the Battle of Muktsar in 1705.\nReligion: Sikhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-2315953@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260114
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260118
SUMMARY:Pongal 
DESCRIPTION:Pongal is a four-day harvest festival celebrated by Tamil people in Southern India and Sri Lanka\, dedicated to the Hindu Sun God Surya\, thanking Surya for agricultural abundance. Also known as Lohri in Northern India.\nReligion: Hinduism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-9685334@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260116
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260117
SUMMARY:Lailat al Miraj
DESCRIPTION:Lailat al Miraj is the observance of Prophet Muhammad’s Night Journey comprised of two parts: a physical journey from Mecca to Jerusalem (al Isra)\, and a spiritual journey\, his ascension to heaven (al Miraj) and return the same night.\nReligion: Islam
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-7965580@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260119
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260120
SUMMARY:Feast of Epiphany [Orthodox]
DESCRIPTION:Feast of Epiphany\, or Theophany\, commemorates Christ's baptism by John the Baptist in the River Jordan\, and the manifestation of God in human form as Jesus Christ. Celebrated 12 days after Orthodox Christmas (Nativity).\nReligion: Christianity
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-3640435@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260203
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260204
SUMMARY:Lailat al Bara'ah
DESCRIPTION:Lailat al Bara'ah\, meaning night of salvation\, is one of the most sacred nights on the Islamic calendar where practitioners seek forgiveness for sins. Shia and Sunni interpretations may vary on the meaning of this date.\nReligion: Islam
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-3529926@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260210
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260211
SUMMARY:Losar / Tibetan New Year
DESCRIPTION:Tibetan New Year is a 15-day festival celebrated on various dates depending on location (ie Tibet\, Bhutan\, Nepal and India). During this time\, people visit monasteries\, make offerings\, receive blessings\, and take part in various activities symbolising purification and welcoming in the new year. Also known as Losar.\nReligion: Buddhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-2951540@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260216
SUMMARY:Nirvana Day
DESCRIPTION:Nirvana Day celebrates the day when the Buddha is said to have achieved complete enlightenment (Parinirvana) upon the death of his physical body at the age of 80. Also known as 'Parinirvana Day'.\nReligion: Buddhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-6229221@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260216
SUMMARY:MahaShivaratri
DESCRIPTION:MahaShivaratri is a festival celebrating the Hindu deity\, Lord Shiva. According to legend\, this is the night when Lord Shiva performs the cosmic dance of creation\, preservation and destruction. Also known as 'Great Night of Shiva'.\nReligion: Hinduism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-5907935@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260217
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260218
SUMMARY:Lunar New Year 
DESCRIPTION:Lunar New Year marks the beginning of the new year based on the lunar or lunisolar calendar. Also known as Chinese New Year or Spring Festival in China\, Tet in Vietnam\, Seollal in South Korea. Date may differ in each country.\nReligion: Buddhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-1294293@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260217
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260319
SUMMARY:Ramadan
DESCRIPTION:Ramadan commemorates the revelation of the Qur'an to the Prophet Muhammad. It is the holiest month for Muslims\, who dedicate themselves to prayer\, reading of the Qur’an\, fasting during daylight hours\, and charity to the poor.\nReligion: Islam
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-4784892@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260218
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260403
SUMMARY:Lent
DESCRIPTION:Lent is the period of 40 days (not including Sundays) which comes before Easter\, traditionally a time of fasting and reflection. The 40 days represents the time Jesus spent in the desert overcoming temptation by Satan. In Western Christianity\, it begins on Ash Wednesday and ends on Maundy Thursday.\nReligion: Christianity
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-5324036@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260223
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260404
SUMMARY:Great Lent [Orthodox] 
DESCRIPTION:Great Lent is the period of 40 days which comes before Easter\, traditionally a time of fasting and reflection. The 40 days represents the time Jesus spent in the desert overcoming temptation by Satan. In the Orthodox Church\, Great Lent starts on Clean Monday and ends on the Friday before Lazarus Saturday and Palm Sunday.\nReligion: Christianity
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-2959639@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260303
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260304
SUMMARY:Magha Puja Day
DESCRIPTION:Magha Puja Day commemorates the Buddha's teachings to a spontaneous gathering of 1250 holy men (arahants). Also known as 'Great Assembly Day' or 'Sangha Day'.\nReligion: Buddhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-7457724@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260303
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260314
SUMMARY:Purim
DESCRIPTION:Purim is a joyous festival\, recalling the saving of the Jewish people living in Persia by the courage of a young Jewish woman\, Queen Esther.\nReligion: Judaism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-9333986@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260303
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260304
SUMMARY:Holi
DESCRIPTION:li is a joyous Hindu festival celebrating spring\, the eternal and divine love of the Hindu deities Radha and Krishna\, and Lord Vishnu’s triumph of good over evil. Bonfires are lit and people throw coloured water\, powder and dyes in celebration.\nReligion: Hinduism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-2200657@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260304
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260307
SUMMARY:Hola Mohalla  
DESCRIPTION:Hola Mohalla is a festival started by Guru Gobind Singh Ji\, as a gathering of Sikhs for military exercises\, mock battles\, athletic competitions\, and literary contests.\nReligion: Sikhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-2595319@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260314
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260315
SUMMARY:Sikh New Year
DESCRIPTION:Sikhs who follow the Nanakshahi Calendar consider March 14 as their New Year. The calendar takes its name from Guru Nanak Dev Ji\, the founder of the Sikh faith\, who's birthday is also celebrated on this day. Sikhs who follow the Bikrami calendar consider Vaisakhi as their New Year\, celebrated April 14.\nReligion: Sikhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-5678535@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260316
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260317
SUMMARY:Lailat al Qadr
DESCRIPTION:Lailat al Qadr commemorates the first revelation of the Qur'an to Prophet Muhammad in 610 CE. Also known as 'Night of Power/Destiny'.\nReligion: Islam
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-4766737@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260320
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260321
SUMMARY:Eid ul Fitr
DESCRIPTION:Eid ul Fitr is a celebration marking the end of Ramadan\, the Islamic holy month of fasting. It is a time when families and friends get together\, and a time for giving gifts to the poor. Also known as the festival of the 'Breaking of the Fast'.\nReligion: Islam
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683964-7800934@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260321
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260322
SUMMARY:Naw Ruz
DESCRIPTION:Naw Ruz\, meaning ‘New Day’\, is the Baha’i and Persian New Year\, which occurs on the date of the vernal equinox. The inception of the Baha’i calendar was on 21 March 1844 CE with the declaration of the Bab\, the prophet-herald of the Baha'i faith.\nReligion: Baha'i
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-2903481@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260325
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260326
SUMMARY:Annunciation
DESCRIPTION:Annunciation marks the visit of the angel Gabriel to the Virgin Mary\, during which he told her she would be the mother of Jesus Christ\, the Son of God.\nReligion: Christianity
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-6238980@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260326
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260327
SUMMARY:Rama Navami
DESCRIPTION:Rama Navami is a festival celebrating the birth of Lord Rama\, the seventh incarnation of the Hindu God Vishnu and hero of the religious epic poem 'The Ramayana'.\nReligion: Hinduism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-3286569@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260329
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260405
SUMMARY:Holy Week
DESCRIPTION:Holy week is the last week before Easter. It begins with Palm Sunday (entry of Jesus Christ into Jerusalem) and includes Maundy Thursday (Last Supper)\, Good Friday (Crucifixion) and Easter Saturday (final day of Christ's death).\nReligion: Christianity
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-6525466@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260331
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260401
SUMMARY:Mahavir Jayanti
DESCRIPTION:Mahavir Jayanti celebrates the birth of Lord Mahavira\, the 24th and last enlightened spiritual Master (Tirthankar) in Jainism. Images of Lord Mahavira are paraded through the streets while performing rituals and preaching about Lord Mahavira's teachings.\nReligion: Jainism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-4118159@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260402
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260410
SUMMARY:Pesach
DESCRIPTION:Pesach is an eight-day festival when Jews commemorate the Exodus from their slavery in Egypt. The festival begins with the Seder meal during which time the story of their deliverance is told. Also known as Passover.\nReligion: Judaism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-1024539@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260402
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260406
SUMMARY:Theravada New Year
DESCRIPTION:Theravada New Year is celebrated for three days from the first full moon day in April\, in Theravadin countries like Thailand\, Burma\, Sri Lanka\, Cambodia\, and Lao.\nReligion: Buddhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-8164128@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260403
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260404
SUMMARY:Good/Holy Friday 
DESCRIPTION:Good Friday is a solemn day of mourning and reflection\, commemorating the suffering and crucifixion of Jesus Christ\, considered by Christians to be the Son of God.\nReligion: Christianity
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-9815541@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260405
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260406
SUMMARY:Easter/Pascha
DESCRIPTION:Easter is a celebration commemorating the resurrection of Jesus Christ\, three days after his death by crucifixion.\nReligion: Christianity
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-2707483@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260410
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260411
SUMMARY:Good/Holy Friday [Orthodox]
DESCRIPTION:Commemoration of the suffering and crucifixion of Jesus Christ.\nReligion: Christianity
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-4082290@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260412
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260413
SUMMARY:Easter/Pascha [Orthodox]
DESCRIPTION:The resurrection of Jesus Christ following his death by crucifixion.\nReligion: Christianity
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-9657048@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260414
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260415
SUMMARY:Yom HaShoah
DESCRIPTION:Yom HaShoah\, or Holocaust Remembrance Day\, remembers the victims of the Holocaust\, emphasizing respect for human dignity. Observed by Jewish and other faiths.\nReligion: Judaism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745368247879-41077@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260414
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260415
SUMMARY:Vaisakhi
DESCRIPTION:Vaisakhi is a spring harvest festival that marks the founding of the collective body of all baptised Sikhs (Khalsa) by Guru Gobind Singh Ji.\nReligion: Sikhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-6834537@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260421
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260503
SUMMARY:Ridvan
DESCRIPTION:Ridvan commemorates the twelve-day period that Baha'u'llah\, the founder of the Baha'i faith\, spent in the Garden of Ridvan in the last days of his exile in Baghdad\, and declared himself the Promised One\, as prophesied by the Bab.\nReligion: Baha'i
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-1047771@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260501
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260502
SUMMARY:Vesak / Buddha Day
DESCRIPTION:Vesak is a major Buddhist festival\, celebrating the birth\, enlightenment\, and death of the Buddha. Also known as 'Vishakha Puja' or 'Buddha’s Day'.\nReligion: Buddhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-7679449@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260522
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260524
SUMMARY:Shavuot
DESCRIPTION:Shavuot celebrates the revelation of the Torah on Mount Sinai. Also known as Feast of Weeks.\nReligion: Judaism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-3204907@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260524
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260525
SUMMARY:Declaration of the Bab
DESCRIPTION:Declaration of the Bab commemorates when The Bab heralded the arrival of Baha'ullah\, the founder of the Baha'i faith.\nReligion: Baha'i
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-3642807@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260524
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260525
SUMMARY:Pentecost
DESCRIPTION:Pentecost commemorates the descent of the Holy Spirit upon the disciples of Jesus\, fifty days after Easter\, and the beginning of the Christian Church.\nReligion: Christianity
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-4114691@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260527
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260531
SUMMARY:Eid Al Adha
DESCRIPTION:Eid Al Adha is a major festival commemorating Ibrahim's (Abraham) willingness to sacrifice his son as an act of submission to God's command. Also known as 'Feast of Sacrifice' and one of the two main Islamic festivals\, the other being Eid al Fitr.\nReligion: Islam
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-1940448@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260529
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260530
SUMMARY:Ascension of Baha'ullah
DESCRIPTION:Ascension of Baha'ullah observes the anniversary of the death of Baha'u'llah\, the founder of the Baha'i faith\, on May 29 1892 CE.\nReligion: Baha'i
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-6500202@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260531
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260601
SUMMARY:Saga Dawa Duchen
DESCRIPTION:Saga Dawa Duchen\, an important holy day for Tibetan Buddhists\, commemorates the birth\, enlightenment\, and death of the Buddha.\nReligion: Buddhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-9974814@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260616
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260617
SUMMARY:Martyrdom of Guru Arjun Dev Ji
DESCRIPTION:Martyrdom of Guru Arjun Dev Ji (1563-1606 CE)\, commemorates the death of the fifth Sikh Guru\, who was the first martyr Guru. He was responsible for the compilation of the Sikh scriptures (Guru Granth Sahib) and helped to build the Golden Temple at Amritsar.\nReligion: Sikhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-5373504@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260616
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260617
SUMMARY:Hijra
DESCRIPTION:Hijra commemorates the journey that Muhammad made from Mecca to Medina in 622 CE to flee persecution and set up the first Muslim community founded on Islamic principles. Also signifies the becoming of the Islamic New Year.\nReligion: Islam
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-3033843@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260626
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260627
SUMMARY:Ashura
DESCRIPTION:Ashura\, for Sunni Muslims\, commemorates when Prophet Moses (Musa) and his followers were saved by crossing the Red Sea. For Shia Muslims\, it is a day of mourning for the martyrdom of Imam Husayn\, grandson of Prophet Muhammad\, in 680 CE.\nReligion: Islam
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-9600666@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260710
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260711
SUMMARY:Martyrdom of the Bab
DESCRIPTION:Martyrdom of the Bab commemorates the anniversary of the execution of The Bab (Siyyid 'Ali- Muhammad)\, the prophet-herald of the Baha'i Faith\, in 1850 CE.\nReligion: Baha'i
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-5817466@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260723
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260724
SUMMARY:Tisha B'Av
DESCRIPTION:Tisha B'av is a day of mourning to remember events such as the destruction of the First Temple and Second Temple in Jerusalem.\nReligion: Judaism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-4342074@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260729
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260730
SUMMARY:Asalha Puja
DESCRIPTION:Asalha Puja commemorates the Buddha's first teaching and is recognised as the beginning of Buddhism and the monastic community of monks and nuns (Sangha). Also known as Dharma Day.\nReligion: Buddhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-7776677@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Assumption of the Blessed Virgin Mary
DESCRIPTION:Assumption of the Blessed Virgin Mary commemorates when the Blessed Virgin Mary\, mother of Jesus\, was taken (assumed) into heaven\, body and soul. Also known as the Feast of the Assumption.\nReligion: Christianity
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-3437081@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Ullambana
DESCRIPTION:Ullambana\, is a Mahayana Buddhist ritual of making merit for the deceased. Lay devotees make offerings on behalf of their ancestors and dedicate the merit towards relieving their suffering. Also known as 'Ancestor Day' or 'Obon'.\nReligion: Buddhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-9952470@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Raksha Bandhan
DESCRIPTION:Raksha Bandhan is a festival celebrating a brother-sister like relationship between relatives or biologically unrelated. Also known as Rakhi.\nReligion: Hinduism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-9507316@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260905
SUMMARY:Krishna Janmashtami
DESCRIPTION:Krishna Janmashtami commemorates the birth of the Hindu deity Krishna\, considered to be the eighth incarnation (avatar) of the Hindu God Vishnu. Worship of Krishna is characteristically expressed in song and dance.\nReligion: Hinduism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-1167419@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260908
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Paryushana
DESCRIPTION:Paryushana\, which means to stay in one place\, is an eight-day festival signifying a time of fasting\, reflection and repentance for nuns\, monks and Jain practitioners from the Swetamber sect.\nReligion: Jainism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-2770269@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260912
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:Rosh Hashanah
DESCRIPTION:Rosh Hashanah\, the Jewish New Year festival\, is the beginning of the holiest time of the year for Jews\, and the anniversary of the creation of the world. Marked by the blowing of the horn (shofar) which begins the ten days of penitence culminating in Yom Kippur (Day of Atonement).\nReligion: Judaism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-1211538@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Ganesh Chaturthi
DESCRIPTION:Ganesh Chaturthi celebrates the birthday of the Hindu deity Lord Ganesh\, who has the head of an elephant and known as the remover of obstacles.\nReligion: Hinduism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-2468573@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Samvatsari
DESCRIPTION:Samvatsari is a day where Jains from the Swetamber sect offer and seek forgiveness for any wrong actions committed knowingly or unknowingly. Also known as the 'Festival of Forgiveness'.\nReligion: Jainism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-7687204@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Daslakshana
DESCRIPTION:Daslakshana is a ten-day festival celebrated by Jains from the Digambara sect\, honouring the ten cardinal virtues of the soul: forgiveness\, humility\, straight forwardness\, contentment\, truth\, sensual restraint\, austerities\, charity\, non-possessiveness\, and celibacy.\nReligion: Jainism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-5772701@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260921
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260922
SUMMARY:Yom Kippur
DESCRIPTION:Yom Kippur is the holiest day of the year for the Jewish people\, characterized by fasting\, intensive prayer\, repentance and forgiveness. Also known as Day of Atonement.\nReligion: Judaism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-2212807@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260926
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261003
SUMMARY:Sukkot
DESCRIPTION:Sukkot is an eight-day harvest festival which recalls the 40 years the Jews spent in the wilderness on the way from slavery in Egypt to freedom in the Promised Land. The name refers to the temporary hut or booth (sukkot) used for eating meals and for socialising. Also known as the Feast of Booths.\nReligion: Judaism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-4023389@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:Kshamavani
DESCRIPTION:Kshamavani is a day where Jains from the Digambara sect offer and seek forgiveness for any wrong actions committed knowingly or unknowingly. Also known as 'Forgiveness Day'.\nReligion: Jainism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-6380662@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261003
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261004
SUMMARY:Shemini Atzeret
DESCRIPTION:Shemini Atzeret\, literally the '8th day of assembly'\, marks the end of Sukkot and the beginning of the rainy season in Israel and\, therefore includes the year’s first prayer for rain.\nReligion: Judaism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-7884086@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:Simchat Torah
DESCRIPTION:Simchat Torah is a joyous festival in which the annual cycle of reading the Torah is over\, and the next cycle begins again (the reading moves from the last words of Deuteronomy to the first ones of Genesis). The celebration typically includes singing\, dancing\, and parading Torah scrolls around the synagogue.\nReligion: Judaism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-5979154@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261011
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261020
SUMMARY:Navaratri
DESCRIPTION:Navaratri\, which literally means 'nine nights'\, is a nine-day festival worshipping and honouring the Goddess/Divine Mother and her energy (Shakti). Festival includes dancing as people celebrate various aspects of the feminine.\nReligion: Hinduism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-1076858@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
SUMMARY:Dussehra
DESCRIPTION:Dussehra commemorates the triumph of the Hindu deity Lord Rama over the demon king Ravana\, symbolizing the victory of good over evil.\nReligion: Hinduism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-6470319@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
SUMMARY:Conferment of Guruship to Guru Granth Sahib
DESCRIPTION:Conferment of Guruship to Guru Granth Sahib celebrates Guru Gobind Singh Ji’s declaration in 1708 CE that\, instead of having another human Guru\, from now on Sikhs would regard the scripture\, the Guru Granth Sahib\, as their Guru.\nReligion: Sikhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-1085594@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Kathina
DESCRIPTION:Kathina is a Theravadan Buddhist festival which comes at the end of the three-month rainy season retreat (Vassa). It is a time where the laity express gratitude to the monks and nuns by offering them new robes and other necessities. Also\, a time for Buddhists to give money to the poor or needy\, called giving alms.\nReligion: Buddhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683966-5968621@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:All Saints Day
DESCRIPTION:All Saints Day honours exemplary Christians who achieved sainthood\, especially those not having a special day. For many Christian denominations\, all Saints Day is a remembrance of departed Christian people of any time and place.\nReligion: Christianity
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-5649323@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Diwali
DESCRIPTION:Diwali is one of the most celebrated Hindu festivals\, commemorating the victory of good over evil. Diwali means 'row of lamps/lights' and refers to the rows of lamps celebrants place around their homes or on top of temples. Also known as 'Festival of Lights'.\nReligion: Hinduism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-1268544@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Bandi Chhor Divas (Diwali)
DESCRIPTION:Bandi Chhor Divas\, or 'The Celebration of Freedom'\, commemorates the release in 1619 CE from prison of Sri Guru Hargobind Ji\, the sixth Sikh Guru.\nReligion: Sikhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683965-8442173@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261110
SUMMARY:Mahavira Nirvana (Diwali)
DESCRIPTION:Mahavira Nirvana is the day Lord Mahavira\, the 24th and last enlightened spiritual Master (Tirthankar)\, gave his last teachings and attained ultimate liberation (Nirvana).\nReligion: Jainism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683966-2832372@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Birth of the Bab
DESCRIPTION:Birth of the Bab is the birth anniversary of The Bab\, born Siyyid 'Ali- Muhammad in 1819 CE\, regarded as the prophet-herald of the Baha'i faith.\nReligion: Baha'i
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683966-1555732@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261111
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261112
SUMMARY:Birth of Baha'ullah
DESCRIPTION:Birth of Baha'ullah is the birth anniversary of Baha'u'llah\, born Mirza Husayn-'Ali in 1817 CE\, who is the founder of the Baha'i faith.\nReligion: Baha'i
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683966-5925042@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261124
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261125
SUMMARY:Birth of Guru Nanak Dev Sahib Ji
DESCRIPTION:Observes the birth of Sri Guru Nanak Dev Sahib Ji\, the founder of the Sikh religion\, born in 1469 CE. An accomplished poet\, 974 of his hymns are part of the Sikh scriptures (Guru Granth Sahib).\nReligion: Sikhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683966-2286788@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261124
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261125
SUMMARY:Martyrdom of Guru Tegh Bahadur Ji
DESCRIPTION:Martyrdom of Guru Tegh Bahadur Ji commemorates the execution of Guru Tegh Bahadur (1621-1675 CE)\, the ninth Sikh Guru\, for his defense of the Sikh faith and for upholding the right to practice religious freedom.\nReligion: Sikhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683966-7385728@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:Day of the Covenant
DESCRIPTION:Day of the Covenant commemorates Baha'u'llah's appointment of his eldest son\, Abdu'l-Baha\, as the leader of the Baha'i community after his passing.\nReligion: Baha'i
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683966-7598551@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261128
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261129
SUMMARY:Ascension of Abdu’l‑Baha
DESCRIPTION:Ascension of Abdu'l‑Baha commemorates the passing of Abdu'l-Baha in 1921 CE\, the eldest son and successor of Baha'u'llah\, the founder of the Baha'i faith\nReligion: Baha'i
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683966-5842217@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261129
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261225
SUMMARY:Advent
DESCRIPTION:Advent is the period leading up to Christmas. It begins on the fourth Sunday before Christmas (Advent Sunday) and continues through to December 24th (Christmas Eve). In Western churches\, Advent Sunday marks the beginning of Christian liturgical year.\nReligion: Christianity
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683966-2881466@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261213
SUMMARY:Hanukkah
DESCRIPTION:Hanukkah is an eight-day festival commemorating the recapture and rededication of the Temple in Jerusalem over occupying forces in 165 BCE. Also known as the Feast of Lights.\nReligion: Judaism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683966-8566632@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261208
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261209
SUMMARY:Bodhi Day
DESCRIPTION:Bodhi Day commemorates the day the Buddha\, Siddhartha Gautama\, reached enlightenment under the Bodhi tree around 596 BCE. Also celebrated on lunar date which can fall in January.\nReligion: Buddhism
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20250423T075053Z
UID:1745362683966-6282189@ical.marudot.com
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261225
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261226
SUMMARY:Christmas
DESCRIPTION:Christmas is the celebration of the birth of Jesus Christ\, who is considered by Christians to be the Son of God\, and the savior of all people. [Celebrated on January 7th by some Orthodox Churches].\nReligion: Christianity
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR